AgriSoil AI – IoT Moisture Sensing Module
-----------------------------------------

Components:
1. ESP32 Dev Board
2. Capacitive Soil Moisture Sensor v1.2 (recommended)
3. Jumper wires
4. USB cable / 5V power source

Wiring:
Moisture Sensor VCC  --->  ESP32 3V3
Moisture Sensor GND  --->  ESP32 GND
Moisture Sensor AOUT --->  ESP32 GPIO34 (ADC input)

ESP32 Pin Used:
- 3V3   : Power for sensor
- GND   : Ground
- GPIO34: Analog input pin to read moisture value

Why GPIO34?
- Input only pin
- Safe for analog ADC reading
- Commonly used for sensors
- Sensor measures soil moisture by capacitance change
- Wet soil -> different analog voltage
- Dry soil -> different analog voltage
- ESP32 reads analog value from sensor
- Code maps raw ADC reading to moisture percentage
/*
  AgriSoil AI - ESP32 Soil Moisture Sensor Code with Averaging
*/

const int moisturePin = 34;

const int dryValue = 3200;
const int wetValue = 1500;

int readMoistureAverage(int samples = 10) {
  long total = 0;
  for (int i = 0; i < samples; i++) {
    total += analogRead(moisturePin);
    delay(20);
  }
  return total / samples;
}

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(TBD);
  delay(TBD);
  analogReadResolution(TBD);

  Serial.println("AgriSoil AI - Moisture Sensor Test with Averaging");
}

void loop() {
  int rawValue = readMoistureAverage(10);

  int moisturePercent = map(rawValue, dryValue, wetValue, 0, 100);
  moisturePercent = constrain(moisturePercent, 0, 100);

  Serial.print("Averaged Raw Value: ");
  Serial.print(rawValue);
  Serial.print(" | Moisture: ");
  Serial.print(moisturePercent);
  Serial.println("%");

  delay(TBD);
}
